**Correct Approach:**
The area of a triangle given vertices (x1, y1), (x2, y2), (x3, y3) can be calculated using the shoelace formula:
Area = (1/2) |x1(y2 - y3) + x2(y3 - y1) + x3(y1 - y2)|.
Plugging in the points (0, 0), (-1, 1), (3, 3):
Area = (1/2) |0(1 - 3) + (-1)(3 - 0) + 3(0 - 1)| = (1/2) |0 - 3 - 3| = (1/2) * 6 = 3 square units.

